# Run records are the evidence docs/evaluation.md points at, so the JSON summaries are
# tracked. The per-document score arrays are tracked too: they are 36 KB each, and they
# are what lets anyone re-run the paired bootstrap and the McNemar test on a laptop
# without a GPU. Checkpoints, corpora and logs stay out.
#
# "*" ignores directories as well as files, and git will not descend into an ignored
# directory, so "!*.json" alone never reached reports/experiments/scaling/ or
# reports/experiments/profile/. "!*/" is what lets git look inside them.
*
!*/
!.gitkeep
!.gitignore
!*.json
!ood_scores_*.npz
*.pt
*.safetensors
*.log

# Chrome traces are tens of MB and are regenerated by scripts/profile_train_step.py.
# The committed evidence is the ranked *_summary.json next to them.
*_trace.json
